{"metadata":{"description":"Cross-surface action binding and replay parity evidence for DeepSeek Harness","id":"gh:1333692460","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-action-parity","slug":"dongsheng123132/dsh-action-parity","topics":["action-parity","ai-agent","conformance","cross-surface","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Cross-surface action binding and replay parity evidence for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH Action Parity"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Maintainer / Author：He Fangsheng (贺方升 / 贺去病; also known as Dosen) · hequbing.com**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Evidence that a business action is implemented once and reached consistently from CLI, MCP and GUI s"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"urfaces in DeepSeek Harness. Version 0.2 adds a formal Codex plugin manifest, a proof-only MCP serve"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"r, real ToolRuntime smoke coverage and a namespace-export regression test for the stock DSH Web load"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"real ToolRuntime smoke coverage and a namespace-export regression test for the stock DSH Web loader."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This plugin does not execute business actions and does not test buttons by pixels. It verifies a man"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ifest of stable Action IDs, content-addressed action-core and binding declarations, and structural r"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"eplay observations produced by each interface."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it verifies"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- every CLI, MCP and GUI binding names the same stable `actionId` and `coreActionId`;
- GUI bindings"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" expose `data-action-id:<actionId>` while CLI and MCP use stable machine identifiers;
- core modules"},{"id":"p7s3","text":", binding declarations and replay fixtures still match their declared SHA-256;
- the same fixture yi"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"elds the same result digest, success state and state-version transition on every surface;
- stale mu"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"tations fail closed with `STALE_STATE` and do not advance state;
- confirmation-required actions enf"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"orce confirmation on every surface;
- missing/stale evidence and every parity failure are disclosed "},{"id":"p7s7","text":"in a deterministic content-addressed report."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Inputs containing secret-, prompt-, chat-, raw input/output-, argv-, stdout- or stderr-shaped fields"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" are rejected. Paths must remain inside `workspaceRoot`; symlink inputs and output directories are r"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ejected. Only the explicit `artifactDir` is written, with atomic publication and SHA-256 read-back v"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"y the explicit `artifactDir` is written, with atomic publication and SHA-256 read-back verification."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The bundle registers `dsh_action_parity_inspect` and `dsh_action_parity_verify`."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The package deliberately exposes only namespace exports and declares standard ToolDefinition objects"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" without bundling a second DSH runtime. This keeps it loadable by the stock DSH Web profile while pr"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"eserving the same shared, interface-free verification core for DSH tools, CLI and MCP."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## CLI"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Exit code `0` means verified, `2` means evidence was processed but parity failed, and `1` means inva"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"lid or unsafe input."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"See `examples/basic` for a mutation whose CLI, MCP and GUI bindings share one core, including succes"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"s and stale-state fixtures."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Codex and proof-only MCP"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The formal Codex bundle exposes two stdio MCP tools:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- `action_parity_manifest_inspect` validates an inline manifest;
- `action_parity_observations_verif"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"y` checks inline JSONL envelopes against that manifest."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"These MCP tools are intentionally proof-only: they do not read the filesystem, dereference declarati"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"on paths, execute actions or write artifacts. Therefore declaration content hashes are reported as n"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ot verified. Use the DSH tools or CLI when you need workspace-bounded file hash verification and an "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"atomically published, read-back-verified report."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}
